Puppeteer-cluster is a library designed to facilitate running multiple instances of Puppeteer concurrently, which is particularly useful for tasks like web crawling or scraping that involve processing several pages simultaneously. Below is an example of how to implement a web crawler using Puppeteer-cluster in Node.js:

1. Install Puppeteer-cluster:
   - Execute the command `npm install puppeteer-cluster` in your terminal.

2. Create a new JavaScript file and import Puppeteer and Puppeteer-cluster at the beginning:
```javascript
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');
const { Cluster } = require('puppeteer-cluster');
```

3. Define a function to be executed for each page processed by the cluster:
```javascript
async function crawlPage({ page, data }) {
  const result = await page.evaluate(() => {
    const elements = document.querySelectorAll('YOUR_SELECTOR');
    const results = [];
    for (let element of elements) {
      results.push({
        title: element.querySelector('YOUR_TITLE_SELECTOR').textContent,
        url: element.querySelector('YOUR_URL_SELECTOR').getAttribute('href')
      });
    }
    return results;
  });
  data.push(result);
}
```

4. Define a function to initiate the crawler:
```javascript
async function runCrawler(url) {
  const data = [];
  const cluster = await Cluster.launch({
    concurrency: Cluster.CONCURRENCY_PAGE,
    maxConcurrency: 10,
  });
  await cluster.task(async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto(url);
    await crawlPage({ page, data });
  });
  await cluster.idle();
  await cluster.close();
  console.log(data);
}
```

5. Execute the `runCrawler` function with the desired URL:
```javascript
runCrawler('https://example.com');
