2. Install the Flurry SDK by following the instructions in the Flurry documentation. This usually involves adding the Flurry framework to your Xcode project and importing the Flurry header file in your source code.
3. Initialize the Flurry SDK in your app's `didFinishLaunchingWithOptions` method using your API key:
```
#import <Flurry.h>

- (BOOL)application:(UIApplication *)application didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:(NSDictionary *)launchOptions {
  [Flurry startSession:@"YOUR_API_KEY_HERE"];
  return YES;
}
```
4. To track an event, use the `logEvent:` method and specify the event name:
```
[Flurry logEvent:@"ButtonTapped"];
```
You can also include additional parameters with the event:
```
[Flurry logEvent:@"ButtonTapped" withParameters:@{@"ButtonColor": @"Red"}];
```
You can then use the Flurry dashboard to view and analyze the tracked events in your app.

