To play the link from Castlabs SDK in an Android application using Kotlin, follow these steps:

1. Add the Castlabs SDK dependency to your project. Include it in your project-level `build.gradle` file:
```python
allprojects {
    repositories {
        maven { url "https://artifacts.castlabs.com/artifactory/castlabs" }
    }
}
```
And in your app-level `build.gradle` file:
```python
dependencies {
    implementation "com.castlabs:castlabs-sdk:4.1.0"
}
```
2. Create an API service interface using Retrofit to make a GET request to the `/api/MediaStorage/GetCookies` endpoint to retrieve cookies. Here is an example:
```kotlin
interface ApiService {

    @GET("/api/MediaStorage/GetCookies")
    suspend fun getCookies(): ResponseBody

}
```
3. In your activity or fragment, call the `getCookies()` function using Retrofit and extract the cookies. Example:
```kotlin
val retrofit = Retrofit.Builder()
    .baseUrl("https://your-api-url.com")
    .build()

val apiService = retrofit.create(ApiService::class.java)
val cookies = apiService.getCookies().headers().get("Set-Cookie")
```
4. Add the cookies and Key-Pair-Id query parameter or cookie value to the `PlayerConfig` object when initializing the Castlabs player. Example:
```css
