The following is a sample implementation for converting SQL queries to MongoDB queries in Java:

```java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;
import java.util.regex.Matcher;

public class SQLtoMongoDB {
    // Regular expression for extracting fields and values from SQL WHERE clause
    private static final String WHERE_REGEX = "(\\w+)\\s*(=|<|>|<=|>=|!=)\\s*(\\w+)";

    // Method to convert SQL query to MongoDB query
    public static List<String> convert(String sql) {
        List<String> mongoQueries = new ArrayList<>();

        // Extract fields and values from SQL WHERE clause
        Pattern pattern = Pattern.compile(WHERE_REGEX);
        Matcher matcher = pattern.matcher(sql);
        while (matcher.find()) {
            String field = matcher.group(1);
            String operator = matcher.group(2);
            String value = matcher.group(3);

            // Convert SQL operator to MongoDB operator
            switch (operator) {
                case "=":
                    operator = "$eq";
                    break;
                case "<":
                    operator = "$lt";
                    break;
                case ">":
                    operator = "$gt";
                    break;
                case "<=":
                    operator = "$lte";
                    break;
                case ">=":
                    operator = "$gte";
                    break;
                case "!=":
                    operator = "$ne";
                    break;
            }

            // Create MongoDB query
            String mongoQuery = String.format("{%s: {%s: %s}}", field, operator, value);
            mongoQueries.add(mongoQuery);
        }

        return mongoQueries;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Sample SQL query
        String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE age > 30 AND gender = 'male'";

        // Convert to MongoDB query
        List<String> mongoQueries = convert(sql);
        System.out.println(mongoQueries);  // Output: [{age: {$gt: 30}}, {gender: {$eq: "male"}}]
    }
}
```

This implementation uses a regular expression to extract fields and values from the SQL WHERE clause and converts the SQL operators to their corresponding MongoDB operators. It returns a list of MongoDB queries that can be used to filter documents in a collection. This example is simplified and may not cover all possible SQL query variations. Additional logic and error handling may be necessary for more complex queries in practical applications.

