Consider a method that takes a list of integers and calculates the sum of all even numbers in the list. Here's how you might implement this using a `List<int>`:
```csharp
public static int SumEvenNumbers(List<int> numbers)
{
    int sum = 0;
    foreach (int number in numbers)
    {
        if (number % 2 == 0)
        {
            sum += number;
        }
    }
    return sum;
}
```
If you want this method to work with various list implementations, such as `LinkedList<int>` or `ObservableCollection<int>`, you can modify it to use `IList<int>`:
```csharp
public static int SumEvenNumbers(IList<int> numbers)
{
    int sum = 0;
    foreach (int number in numbers)
    {
        if (number % 2 == 0)
        {
            sum += number;
        }
    }
    return sum;
}
```
This allows the method to be called with any `IList<int>` implementation, such as a `List<int>` or a `LinkedList<int>`:
```csharp
