int sum1 = SumEvenNumbers(numbersList); // returns 6

LinkedList<int> numbersLinkedList = new LinkedList<int>(new[] { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 });
int sum2 = SumEvenNumbers(numbersLinkedList); // returns 6
```
By using `IList<int>` instead of `List<int>`, the code becomes more adaptable, allowing it to work with different list implementations.

