To create a component that converts between different temperature units using React Hooks, you can utilize the `useState` hook to manage the state of the input temperature and the selected temperature unit. The `useEffect` hook can be used to perform the conversion whenever there is a change in the input temperature or the selected temperature unit.

Here is an example implementation of this component:
```javascript
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const TemperatureInput = () => {
  const [inputTemperature, setInputTemperature] = useState(0);
  const [selectedUnit, setSelectedUnit] = useState('celsius');
  const [convertedTemperature, setConvertedTemperature] = useState(0);

  const convertTemperature = () => {
    if (selectedUnit === 'celsius') {
      setConvertedTemperature((inputTemperature * 9) / 5 + 32);
    } else if (selectedUnit === 'fahrenheit') {
      setConvertedTemperature(((inputTemperature - 32) * 5) / 9);
    }
  };

  useEffect(() => {
    convertTemperature();
  }, [inputTemperature, selectedUnit]);

  return (
    <div>
      <input
        type="number"
        value={inputTemperature}
        onChange={event => setInputTemperature(event.target.value)}
      />
      <select value={selectedUnit} onChange={event => setSelectedUnit(event.target.value)}>
        <option value="celsius">Celsius</option>
        <option value="fahrenheit">Fahrenheit</option>
      </select>
      <p>{convertedTemperature}</p>
    </div>
  );
};
```
In this example, the `TemperatureInput` component uses the `useState` hook to manage the input temperature, the selected temperature unit, and the converted temperature. The `convertTemperature` function performs the conversion based on the selected unit. The `useEffect` hook ensures that the conversion function is called whenever the input temperature or the selected unit changes, updating the component with the new converted temperature.

