3. Use the `httpClientProvider` to provide the HTTP client to your app's components. You can use `Consumer` to retrieve the client and use it in your widgets or services. For example, you can create a widget that fetches data from a remote API using the HTTP client like this:
```dart
import 'dart:convert';

import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter_riverpod/flutter_riverpod.dart';
import 'package:http/http.dart' as http;

final httpClientProvider = Provider<http.Client>((ref) {
  return http.Client();
});

final dataProvider = FutureProvider<String>((ref) async {
  final client = ref.watch(httpClientProvider);
  final response =
      await client.get(Uri.parse('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/todos/1'));

  return json.decode(response.body)['title'];
});

